<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells 133 trln lira 2-year bonds.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells 133 trln lira 2-year bonds.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey sold 133 trillion lira of inflation-indexed, two-year bonds at 22 percent risk premium on Tuesday, compared to 109.8 trillion lira sale and 24 percent risk premium in the inflation-indexed bond auction on April 1.</p>
<p>Results on page  CBTI.</p>
<p>	Maturity		    : April 9, 1999</p>
<p>	Amount			: 133.0 trln lira</p>
<p>	Bid amount		  : 218.9 trln lira</p>
<p>	Risk premium		: 22 percent</p>
<p>	Payment date		: April 9, 1997</p>
<p>There will be three-month coupon (interest) payments on the bonds.</p>
<p>Banks will pay 131.7 trillion lira to the Treasury for the auction on Wednesday, when they will collect 199 trillion lira from maturing t-bills.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
